---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MIAR Privacy Notice"
  description="Privacy notice for the public MIAR website and request-access form."
  current="privacy"
>
  <main class="subpage-shell legal-document-shell">
    <header class="legal-document-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>How the public MIAR site handles submitted information.</h1>
      <div class="legal-document-meta">
        <span>Effective 30 July 2026</span>
        <span>Public website and request-access form</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-document">
      <aside>
        <p>This notice is deliberately limited to the public website.</p>
        <a href="/terms/">Website terms</a>
        <a href="/legal/">Legal overview</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="legal-document-body">
        <section>
          <h2>Scope</h2>
          <p>
            This notice applies when you visit the public MIAR website or submit its
            request-access form. A pilot, evaluation, customer deployment, or other product
            engagement may be covered by separate privacy and data-handling terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Information you submit</h2>
          <p>The request-access form may collect:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your name, work email, organization, and role.</li>
            <li>Your selected workflow, operating focus, evaluation timing, and use-case notes.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Do not submit classified, export-controlled, operationally sensitive, or other
            restricted information through the public form.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Technical request information</h2>
          <p>
            The site records the submission time, source path, referrer, browser user agent,
            and approximate country, region, and city supplied with the request by Cloudflare.
            This information supports access review, abuse prevention, and site security.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How the information is used</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To assess the organization, use case, and jurisdiction associated with a request.</li>
            <li>To contact the requester where a follow-up is appropriate.</li>
            <li>To maintain a record of inbound requests.</li>
            <li>To detect misuse, reduce spam, and enforce access restrictions.</li>
            <li>To comply with law or respond to a valid legal request.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Who may access it</h2>
          <p>Access is limited to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>ReachDefence personnel responsible for site administration, access review, security, or follow-up.</li>
            <li>Service providers or contractors where access is necessary to host, secure, or maintain the site.</li>
            <li>Professional advisers or authorities where disclosure is required by law or necessary to protect the site and its users.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What is not done with it</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Form submissions are not published.</li>
            <li>Submission data is not sold.</li>
            <li>Submission data is not provided to unrelated parties for advertising.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
          <p>
            Production submissions are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database configured for this
            site. Information may be kept for as long as reasonably needed to review the
            request, maintain operating records, investigate misuse, and meet legal obligations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Restricted jurisdictions</h2>
          <p>
            Country information is used to enforce access-request restrictions. The current
            form rejects requests identified as originating from China or Pakistan. Other
            requests may be refused where identity, intended use, sanctions, export controls,
            or security risk cannot be resolved.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
          <p>
            This notice may be updated when the site, form, or handling practices change. The
            effective date above identifies the current version.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
